WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.705
Atopic dermatitis involves epidermal
barrier dysfunction and immune dysregulation.

00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:08.478
Filaggrin alteration is
one supplied barrier mechanism.

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:10.672
Severe itching drives scratching.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.960
Watch the surface become
disrupted, followed by a thickened

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:15.672
epidermis with repeated scratching.

00:00:16.340 --> 00:00:17.984
The thickening is lichenification.

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.635
Hydration and emollients support barrier care.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:24.847
Distribution changes with age:
infants often have face and

00:00:24.880 --> 00:00:27.860
extensor lesions, while older children favor flexures.
